     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "India's population is about 140 crore.\n\"How do we write that?\" asked Ravi."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "lakh",
     "crore",
     "million"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "In the Indian system we group digits as ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, lakhs and crores. 1 lakh is 100,000 and 1 crore is 100 lakhs, or 10,000,000.\nIn the international system we use millions and billions. 1 million is 10 lakh and 1 billion is 100 crore.\nTo compare numbers, first compare the number of digits, then compare digit by digit from the left."
    }
